# NoteFlow — Cursor Rules

## Stack
- Expo SDK 55 (bare-ish, managed workflow)
- React Native 0.83
- TypeScript (strict mode, no `any`)
- Expo Router v4 (file-based routing)
- Zustand (global state — no Context API for state)
- FlashList from @shopify/flash-list (no FlatList ever)
- Zod (runtime validation of user input and persisted data)
- AsyncStorage via @react-native-async-storage/async-storage

## Project structure
```
app/              # Expo Router screens
  (tabs)/         # Tab navigator group
store/            # Zustand stores only
components/
  items/          # Note-type cards (NoteCard, ChecklistCard, IdeaCard)
  ui/             # Reusable primitives (Button, Input, Sheet, etc.)
types/index.ts    # All shared TypeScript types/interfaces
constants/theme.ts# Design tokens (colors, spacing, typography)
lib/utils.ts      # Pure utility functions (no side effects)
hooks/            # Custom React hooks
docs/             # Project documentation (not shipped)
```

## Naming conventions
- Components: PascalCase (`NoteCard.tsx`)
- Hooks: camelCase prefixed with `use` (`useNotes.ts`)
- Stores: camelCase suffixed with `Store` (`notesStore.ts`)
- Types/interfaces: PascalCase (`AnyNote`, `ChecklistItem`)
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for primitives, PascalCase for objects (`Colors`, `MAX_TITLE_LENGTH`)
- Files: kebab-case for non-component files (`nueva-nota.tsx` follows Expo Router convention)

## Architecture rules
- NEVER use FlatList or ScrollView for long lists — always FlashList
- NEVER use React Context API for global or cross-screen state — use Zustand
- ALWAYS type everything with TypeScript strict. No implicit `any`, no type assertions without comment
- ALWAYS validate data at boundaries (user input, AsyncStorage reads) with Zod
- Stores live in `store/`, one file per domain. No business logic inside components
- Screens are thin: they read from store + call store actions. No local state for persisted data
- `lib/utils.ts` contains pure functions only — no imports from store or components
- Design tokens come exclusively from `constants/theme.ts` — no hardcoded hex values in components
- Use `useColorScheme` from `react-native` to pick between `Colors.dark` and `Colors.light`

## Code style
- Functional components only, no class components
- Prefer named exports over default exports (except Expo Router screens which must be default)
- Keep components under ~150 lines; extract sub-components when exceeded
- No inline styles beyond trivial one-off flex: no StyleSheet.create either — use a styles object at bottom of file
- Prefer `StyleSheet.create` for static styles and inline only for dynamic (theme-based) values

## DO NOT
- Install or suggest expo-navigation (use Expo Router)
- Use `require()` for images in production code; use typed `import`
- Commit secrets or API keys
- Add comments that just restate what the code does
